{"duration_api_ms":39472,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"04bd556c-7c73-49cf-870c-60c1fda05db4","total_cost_usd":0.15783979999999997,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7640,"cache_read_input_tokens":1459,"output_tokens":4821,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2084},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7640,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4821,"cache_read_input_tokens":1459,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7640,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7640},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":4821,"cacheReadInputTokens":1459,"cacheCreationInputTokens":7640,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.15783979999999997,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":2084,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"merged_document\":\"# Freezer Alarm Response - Night Shift\\n\\n## What triggers an alarm\\n\\nEach freezer alarms when the internal temperature rises above its set point for more than 10 minutes. The alarm sounds locally and sends a message to the night phone. The night phone is carried by the weekend duty officer from 18:00 on Friday until 08:00 on Monday.\\n\\n## First response\\n\\nGo to the freezer and read the display. The alarm panel names the unit and shows the temperature that triggered it. Note the unit name: there are three units on this floor and two of them alarm at the same set point. Write the reading and the time in the freezer log before touching anything else. The reading at the moment of arrival is the one the lab needs, and it cannot be recovered later.\\n\\nEvery alarm gets a line in the freezer log whether or not anything was wrong. An alarm with no line in the log is indistinguishable from an alarm nobody attended.\\n\\n## If the door is ajar\\n\\nClose the door and wait 20 minutes. If the temperature falls back below the set point, log it as a door event and no further action is needed. Run a finger along the door seal: ice on the seal holds the door open by a few millimetres and is the usual cause of a slow rise.\\n\\n## If the temperature keeps rising\\n\\nCall the on-call technician if the temperature is still rising 20 minutes after you arrive, and give the unit name, the reading you took on arrival and the reading now. While waiting, do not open the door: opening a door on a failing freezer to check the contents is the most common cause of loss in this building.\\n\\n## Moving contents\\n\\nContents are moved only on the technician's instruction and only into a freezer that already has space at the same set point. Never split a single study's samples across two freezers.\",\"decisions\":[{\"slot\":\"title\",\"candidates\":[{\"text\":\"# Freezer Alarm Response - Night Shift\",\"document\":\"source_a.md\"},{\"text\":\"# Cold Storage Alarm Checklist\",\"document\":\"source_b.md\"}],\"chosen\":\"# Freezer Alarm Response - Night Shift\",\"reason\":\"Base document's title.\"},{\"slot\":\"heading for alarm reading and log recording\",\"candidates\":[{\"text\":\"## First response\",\"document\":\"source_a.md\"},{\"text\":\"## Reading the alarm\",\"document\":\"source_b.md\"},{\"text\":\"## Recording\",\"document\":\"source_b.md\"}],\"chosen\":\"## First response\",\"reason\":\"Base heading already covers reading the display and logging on arrival.\"},{\"slot\":\"heading for door seal check\",\"candidates\":[{\"text\":\"## If the door is ajar\",\"document\":\"source_a.md\"},{\"text\":\"## Check the door seal\",\"document\":\"source_b.md\"}],\"chosen\":\"## If the door is ajar\",\"reason\":\"Base heading covers door problems, including a seal holding it open.\"},{\"slot\":\"heading for escalation\",\"candidates\":[{\"text\":\"## If the temperature keeps rising\",\"document\":\"source_a.md\"},{\"text\":\"## Escalating\",\"document\":\"source_b.md\"}],\"chosen\":\"## If the temperature keeps rising\",\"reason\":\"Base heading serves the same purpose of calling the technician.\"},{\"slot\":\"placement of weekend night phone cover\",\"candidates\":[{\"text\":\"## What triggers an alarm\",\"document\":\"source_a.md\"},{\"text\":\"## Weekend cover\",\"document\":\"source_b.md\"}],\"chosen\":\"## What triggers an alarm\",\"reason\":\"Base section introduces the night phone the cover rule refers to.\"}],\"dispositions\":[{\"segment\":\"a3\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"Each freezer alarms when the internal temperature rises above its set point for more than 10 minutes.\",\"reason\":\"Line-wrapped sentence joined into paragraph prose.\"},{\"segment\":\"a4\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"The alarm sounds locally and sends a message to the night phone.\",\"reason\":\"Line-wrapped sentence joined into paragraph prose.\"},{\"segment\":\"a7\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"Write the reading and the time in the freezer log before touching anything else.\",\"reason\":\"Line-wrapped sentence joined into paragraph prose.\"},{\"segment\":\"a8\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"The reading at the moment of arrival is the one the lab needs, and it cannot be recovered later.\",\"reason\":\"Line wrap joined and comma added.\"},{\"segment\":\"a11\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"If the temperature falls back below the set point, log it as a door event and no further action is needed.\",\"reason\":\"Line-wrapped sentence joined into paragraph prose.\"},{\"segment\":\"a13\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"Call the on-call technician if the temperature is still rising 20 minutes after you arrive\",\"reason\":\"Escalation instruction narrowed by source_b's timing.\"},{\"segment\":\"a14\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"While waiting, do not open the door:\",\"reason\":\"Joined to its explanation with a colon.\"},{\"segment\":\"a15\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"opening a door on a failing freezer to check the contents is the most common cause of loss in this building.\",\"reason\":\"Joined to the preceding instruction; line wraps removed.\"},{\"segment\":\"a17\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"Contents are moved only on the technician's instruction and only into a freezer that already has space at the same set point.\",\"reason\":\"Line-wrapped sentence joined into paragraph prose.\"},{\"segment\":\"a18\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"Never split a single study's samples across two freezers.\",\"reason\":\"Line-wrapped sentence joined into paragraph prose.\"},{\"segment\":\"b1\",\"disposition\":\"superseded\",\"replacement\":\"# Freezer Alarm Response - Night Shift\",\"reason\":\"Base title kept.\"},{\"segment\":\"b2\",\"disposition\":\"superseded\",\"replacement\":\"## First response\",\"reason\":\"Consolidated under base heading.\"},{\"segment\":\"b4\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"Note the unit name: there are three units on this floor and two of them alarm at the same set point.\",\"reason\":\"Line wraps joined; semicolon made a colon.\"},{\"segment\":\"b5\",\"disposition\":\"superseded\",\"replacement\":\"## If the door is ajar\",\"reason\":\"Consolidated under base heading.\"},{\"segment\":\"b6\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"Run a finger along the door seal\",\"reason\":\"Specified the door seal and joined with the next sentence.\"},{\"segment\":\"b7\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"ice on the seal holds the door open by a few millimetres and is the usual cause of a slow rise.\",\"reason\":\"Joined to the seal check; line wrap removed.\"},{\"segment\":\"b8\",\"disposition\":\"superseded\",\"replacement\":\"## If the temperature keeps rising\",\"reason\":\"Consolidated under base heading.\"},{\"segment\":\"b9\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"Call the on-call technician if the temperature is still rising 20 minutes after you arrive, and give the unit name, the reading you took on arrival and the reading now.\",\"reason\":\"Joined with the information to give; line wrap removed.\"},{\"segment\":\"b10\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"Call the on-call technician if the temperature is still rising 20 minutes after you arrive, and give the unit name, the reading you took on arrival and the reading now.\",\"reason\":\"Folded into the escalation sentence.\"},{\"segment\":\"b11\",\"disposition\":\"superseded\",\"replacement\":\"## First response\",\"reason\":\"Consolidated under base heading.\"},{\"segment\":\"b13\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"An alarm with no line in the log is indistinguishable from an alarm nobody attended.\",\"reason\":\"Line-wrapped sentence joined into paragraph prose.\"},{\"segment\":\"b14\",\"disposition\":\"superseded\",\"replacement\":\"## What triggers an alarm\",\"reason\":\"Weekend cover placed with the night phone in base section.\"},{\"segment\":\"b15\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"The night phone is carried by the weekend duty officer from 18:00 on Friday until 08:00 on Monday.\",\"reason\":\"Line-wrapped sentence joined into paragraph prose.\"}],\"mismatch\":\"\"}","ttft_ms":20905,"type":"result","duration_ms":39590,"uuid":"92aa5b4c-859f-4f9b-8972-bafdfaf70